Subject: [PATCH] Retry remotely initiated graceful HTTP/2 GOAWAY in RE RPCs

Base: facebook/buck2 9a1876786f32806f6b65fc51f4c1c3077efc38a5

Tonic maps h2 NO_ERROR to INTERNAL using its RST_STREAM status mapping,
including a remote GOAWAY that retires an HTTP/2 connection normally.
Recognize only the typed remote GOAWAY/NO_ERROR source in the existing
bounded RPC retry policy. Tonic reconnects the pooled channel; do not
retry arbitrary INTERNAL statuses, reset frames, or other GOAWAY reasons.

Regression tests exchange actual HTTP/2 frames and cover successful retry,
exhaustion, genuine INTERNAL errors, other GOAWAY reasons and RST_STREAM.
No dependency, service keepalive limit, or materializer changes.

